  "family": "spatial-mechanism",
  "description": "An exploded plan of the generic hearing room: the wall clock and the exhibit cabinet rise out of their places; the questioner with the lectern stands back from the witness box; the rail and the participants stay. Only the supplied relationships are drawn, edge to edge, with their kind. A tracer follows the supplied traversal; once it reaches the witness box the question slides up the guide and pauses when a seated participant raises a signal; once it reaches the participants, the editable reason card (● intervention raised, as supplied) and the response card (◆ response as supplied, illustrative) travel to the rail and open, and both get the same neutral frame. Fictional and illustrative; no grounds, rule, ruling, outcome, winner or hierarchy is shown.",
